    "title": "pandas.Timedelta.floor — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1662.g0c49719283 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Timedelta.floor#\n\n- \nTimedelta.floor(*freq* )#\n- Return a new Timedelta floored to this resolution. Truncates the Timedelta to the nearest multiple of the given frequency, rounding toward negative infinity. \n  - Parameters:\n    - **freq** str or timedelta\n    - Frequency string or timedelta value indicating the flooring resolution. It uses the same units as class constructor `Timedelta` .\n  - Returns:\n    - Timedelta\n    - A new Timedelta object floored to the specified resolution.\n See also \n  - `Timedelta.ceil`\n  - Ceil the Timedelta to the specified resolution.\n  - `Timedelta.round`\n  - Round the Timedelta to the specified resolution.\n  - `Timestamp.floor`\n  - Similar method for Timestamp objects.\n Examples >>> td = pd.Timedelta('1001ms') >>> td Timedelta('0 days 00:00:01.001000') >>> td.floor('s') Timedelta('0 days 00:00:01') `freq` can also be a timedelta value:>>> td.floor(freq=pd.Timedelta('1s')) Timedelta('0 days 00:00:01')",
    "markdown_length": 954,
